# Text a push to this public repository must not add. One per line: <regex><TAB><why>, a Perl-compatible regular
# expression (a leading (?i) makes it ignore case). The maintainers keep a private list in the same format; see
# .githooks/pre-push. Every pattern here is public, so it names nothing private: it describes a kind of text.

# References to records kept outside this repository
\bplanning#[0-9]+	a reference to an issue in a private repository: describe the work instead
\b[bp]dr-[0-9]{4}\b	a decision record kept outside this repository: describe the decision instead

# Legal self-assessment: write the question and who answers it instead
(?i)\bmay not be permitted by\b	legal self-assessment
(?i)\b(appears?|seems?) to (breach|violate|infringe)\b	legal self-assessment
(?i)\brisks? (breaching|violating|infringing)\b	legal self-assessment

# Pricing: plans of the business are never written here
[$€£][0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?( ?[–-] ?[$€£]?[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?)? ?(/|per |a ) ?(mo|month|year|yr|seat|user)\b	a price: plans of the business are never written here
